# ForgeHaven Suggestions

Saved for later builds from the feature-ideation pass. These are backlog ideas only; not all should be implemented at once.

## Internet-inspired feature categories

### 1. Logistics & Automation
1. Logistics clarity overlay showing item flow direction, throughput, and stuck lanes.
2. Placement preview arrows for every belt, machine, inserter, pipe, and station IO side.
3. Priority splitter with configurable primary and overflow exits.
4. Smart sorter/filter splitter with whitelist, blacklist, and wildcard modes.
5. Lane balancer that equalizes two or three conveyor lines.
6. Underground or bridge belts for compact line crossings.
7. Elevated belts/rails that can pass over ground logistics without mixing.
8. Junction blocks with visible per-lane buffers.
9. Belt throughput tiers with visually distinct speeds and animation.
10. Inserter variants: fast, long, filter, stack, and low-power emergency arm.
11. Logistic drones with pickup/drop rules, repair tasks, and charging limits.
12. Train scheduling UI with route names, station conditions, and cargo filters.
13. Loader/unloader station blocks for high-volume rail transfer.
14. Storage priorities: input-only, output-only, buffer, requester, provider.
15. Item overflow alarms and flashing blocked-belt indicators.
16. Circuit/logic network for enabling machines from sensors and stock counts.
17. Conveyor counters and rate displays for debugging factories.
18. Blueprint copy/paste for repeated production cells.
19. Construction ghost planning with material reservation.
20. Automatic deconstruction planner for obsolete logistics sections.

### 2. Production & Industry
1. Multi-stage recipes with clear ingredient chains and byproducts.
2. Machine modules for speed, efficiency, productivity, and pollution reduction.
3. Maintenance parts and wear so large factories need upkeep logistics.
4. Slag/recycling chain that turns waste into stone, metals, or landfill.
5. Parallel recipe machines with visible selected recipe labels.
6. Low-tech manual fallback stations for anti-softlock recovery.
7. Batch crafting queues for fabricators and assemblers.
8. Quality tiers for advanced parts or weapons.
9. Dedicated foundries for iron, copper, alloys, and crystal composites.
10. Cooling/lubricant requirements for high-tier machines.
11. Production graph screen with bottleneck and surplus summaries.
12. Machine status lights: missing input, output full, no power, no worker.
13. Overclocking that trades speed for heat, wear, or power draw.
14. Recipe unlock tree that changes layouts instead of only raising numbers.
15. Mining productivity research with diminishing returns.
16. Deep-core/resource scanning progression.
17. Dedicated ammo production lines with ammo type variants.
18. Food processing tiers from raw biomass/crops into meals and rations.
19. Robotics chain: drone frames, circuits, batteries, final bots.
20. Late-game ark repair chain using rare crystals and advanced parts.

### 3. Power, Fluids & Environment
1. Power overlay with generation, demand, battery buffer, and brownout causes.
2. Separate electric grids that can be connected/disconnected deliberately.
3. Transformers/substations with larger coverage and overload warnings.
4. Battery priorities and emergency reserve settings.
5. Steam power loop: pump, pipe, boiler, engine, condenser.
6. Fluid overlay with flow direction, pressure, contents, and blocked segments.
7. Tanks with content gauges and priority output settings.
8. Water scarcity/seasonal drought pressure.
9. Weather that affects solar, wind, crops, visibility, and raids.
10. Pollution cloud with flora absorption and enemy-aggression effects.
11. Cleaner machines or scrubbers as late-game mitigation.
12. Heat mechanics for furnaces, boilers, reactors, and cooling systems.
13. Pipe bridges and valves for controllable fluid networks.
14. Sensors for fluid amount, battery charge, sunlight, wind, and pollution.
15. Reactor risk/reward events: leak, meltdown warning, emergency shutdown.
16. Wind turbine spacing efficiency.
17. Solar panel day/night production graph.
18. Terrain water management: canals, floodgates, irrigation, dams.
19. Biome-specific energy modifiers.
20. Environmental restoration projects that reclaim blighted ground.

### 4. Defense & Combat
1. Raid forecast panel showing approximate direction, size, and threat type.
2. Enemy roles: bruiser, ranged raider, sapper, shielded unit, beast swarm.
3. Sappers that target weak walls and power infrastructure.
4. Turret ammo logistics with magazine status and belt-fed reloads.
5. Ammo variants: piercing, incendiary, stun, explosive, cheap scrap rounds.
6. Kill-corridor support blocks: gates, traps, lights, barricades.
7. Repair projector or post-raid repair planner.
8. Colonist draft controls and defensive rally points.
9. Watchtowers requiring operators but no ammo.
10. Guard bot patrol routes and rally commands.
11. Shield generators with visible bubble health and recharge delay.
12. Enemy learning that punishes repeated killbox layouts.
13. Night-raid accuracy penalties reduced by lamps/searchlights.
14. Prisoner capture, medical stabilization, recruitment, or ransom.
15. Wildlife threats that can panic, stampede, or be hunted.
16. Boss/apex raider waves as chapter milestones.
17. Minefields/IEDs with friendly-fire risk.
18. Alarm states that change work priorities during attacks.
19. Fortification materials with tradeoffs: wood, stone, metal, composite.
20. Combat log and damage heatmap after each raid.

