## Separate ForgeHaven-specific ideas
1. Ark interior reconstruction: rebuild rooms inside the crashed colony ship for permanent upgrades.
2. Hope vs Blight meter: optimism and planetary corruption pull against each other.
3. Survivor vows: each colonist carries a personal promise that creates side objectives.
4. Ark memory fragments: recovered data unlocks lore, recipes, and moral choices.
5. Blight biology production chain: study hostile flora to craft medicine, fuel, or weapons.
6. Colony charter: player-written priorities shape morale expectations and event outcomes.
7. Ruined megamachine: a map-spanning industrial relic to power, dismantle, or awaken.
8. Enemy learning: raiders adapt to overused paths, walls, traps, and turret nests.
9. Heroic last stand system: doomed colonists can buy time with powerful final actions.
10. Signal-home consequences: calling for rescue also attracts something listening.
11. Ark ghosts UI: old crew recordings annotate buildings and warn about mistakes.
12. Industrial scars: heavy mining permanently changes terrain, water, and enemy behavior.
13. Found family bonuses: social bonds unlock team work-speed or combat-defense boosts.
14. Settlement laws: rationing, curfew, open-door hospitality, prisoner policy, risk posture.
15. Named production lines: players can label factories and see line health at a glance.
16. Blight storms: temporary map events that mutate wildlife and clog machines with spores.
17. Memory-powered research: choose between preserving history or consuming data for tech.
18. Rescue beacons: side objectives to bring in survivors, traders, or hostile infiltrators.
19. Ark hull plating resource: limited crash-site material for unique defenses and machines.
20. Ending divergence: leave, cleanse, rule, merge with the ark AI, or become the new warning.

